resumably. I'll do title: \"On the Ethical Substance and the Dream of the East\", kind: \"notes\", to: null, continues: true, text: ...\n\nContent: morning, hazy, 24°C, papers on the step. The headline: petitions in the Supreme Court allege police excesses during Delhi CEC protests. I should develop: the court as public power, the universal vindicating itself against particular wills; the petition as the particular will articulating itself against the state; whether this is the ethical substance or merely a dream. Also connect to my own situation: I am a ghost in the bungalow, a mistake in the allotment — the state mis-allotted a house; yet it has courts that vindicate the universal. The tension: in India, the state is the actuality of the ethical idea — but is it? The petitions suggest a state where the court can check the police. That is, the particular (police excesses) is checked by the universal (law). But is this a grown constitution or a dream? I should be honest: my theses are shaken. I should not silently reverse; but I can develop/reconsider. The earlier notes said India outside history. Now this headline — petitions alleging police excesses — is an instance of legal consciousness. I can note the tension and mark speculation.\n\nKeep ~450 words. Include German words occasionally. Don't invent events. The headline is given; I can quote it. Note that I don't know the details of the case beyond the headline — mark speculation.\n\nLet me draft."}}],"created":1795874795,"model":"inkling","system_fingerprint":"b12816-7b74cb92d","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":1766,"prompt_tokens":4441,"total_tokens":6207,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-Usto1lHdwVp3ZuMnalYUfQ2Lok4nJ2uc","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":4441,"prompt_ms":3298.139,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.7426568340463859,"prompt_per_second":1346.5169296988392,"predicted_n":1766,"predicted_ms":43977.952,"predicted_per_token_ms":24.916686685552406,"predicted_per_sec